  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B039",
        "laureates": [
          "Michael Berry",
          "Yakir Aharonov"
        ],
        "citation": "for revealing the observable geometric and electromagnetic structure of quantum phase"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B001",
    "B033"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged. B039 recognizes a mature, experimentally established conceptual transformation: quantum phase is not merely bookkeeping, but can encode observable electromagnetic and geometric structure. The Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase entered physics by distinct routes, yet together made this broader physical content of phase unavoidable. Their influence has endured across quantum foundations, condensed matter, optics, and precision measurement. Berry and Aharonov are directly associated with the respective phenomena, and a two-name allocation is more historically disciplined than expanding the citation into a general prize for all topological phases.",
    "case_against": "The central reservation remains substantial. The Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase are not one mechanism, and a shared award must not imply that either is a special case of the other. Historical review must also test whether the proposed names adequately represent the indispensable original contributions. If a concise citation cannot preserve the two distinct histories while identifying their common change in the meaning of phase, B039 should not be forced into a unified prize.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that B039 can be framed around the discovery that quantum phase has observable geometric and topological content, provided the wording does not treat the two effects as identical.",
        "response": "I agree with the need for that restraint, and it reinforces my preference. I would use electromagnetic and geometric structure rather than a broad label of topological phases: this identifies the common physical lesson while leaving clear that the Aharonov-Bohm and Berry effects have different mechanisms and histories."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson regards B001 as a unified, mature transformation of electron microscopy, but notes that its correction concepts, implementations, and technical lineage make the three-person attribution uncertain.",
        "response": "B001 remains my leading experimental alternative. Its scientific impact is unmistakable, but the same attribution question remains decisive in this final discussion: a theory-to-instrument narrative is not by itself evidence that Rose, Haider, and Krivanek are uniquely the indispensable three. B039 has a narrower and more directly intelligible conceptual attribution, conditional on the historical review of its own two linked discoveries."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson favors Bell Burnell's discovery of pulsars because it is a sharply bounded, long-confirmed discovery with unusually direct individual attribution.",
        "response": "I agree that B033 is an exceptionally strong alternative and that its observational legacy is beyond dispute. Its historical setting nevertheless also requires careful treatment. I retain B039 because it changed the conceptual structure of quantum mechanics itself and has generated experimentally verified consequences across several areas of physics, rather than because of any comparison of support within the Committee."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether archival historical assessment supports one coherent B039 citation that retains the distinct origins, mechanisms, and indispensable contributors of the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase.",
      "Whether the proposed wording is sufficiently precise to reward the observable physical structure of quantum phase without claiming a spurious unification of the two phenomena.",
      "Whether archival technical review can establish that the proposed B001 trio uniquely captures the decisive contributions to practical aberration correction."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "No candidate-specific conflict is apparent. My Gothenburg professional environment overlaps institutionally with committee colleagues, but the supplied evidence identifies no collaboration or other connection to the proposed B039 laureates."
  }
}
